> Cast rays to detect block and entity hits, with voxel-accurate collisions.

name Raycast
slug bookshelf-raycast
version 5.0.0
tags runtime
authors Aksiome

$run: #[command(slash="forbidden",empty="forbidden")] string
$provider: #[id(registry="function",tags="allowed")] string
$blocks: $provider > [block provider](hitbox.md#block-providers) of the blocks the ray hits, such as `#bs.hitbox:get_block/collision`: without it, the ray goes through blocks
$entities: $provider > [entity provider](hitbox.md#entity-providers) of the entities the ray hits, such as `#bs.hitbox:get_entity/sized`: without it, the ray goes through entities
$selector: string > selector arguments the entities must match, such as `tag=my_pack.target`
$max_distance: number @ 0..2047 > distance the ray travels at most, 16 by default

$ray:
  contributors Bafy78
  @position > origin of the ray
  @rotation > direction of the ray
  @dimension > dimension of the ray

$face[bottom, east, north, south, top, west]
$flag[1, 2, 4, 8]

$axis[x]:
  side: west
$axis[y]:
  side: bottom
$axis[z]:
  side: north

$point[entry]:
  verb: enters
  where: a command of the ray
$point[exit]:
  verb: leaves
  where: `on_exit`


feature function cast > Cast a ray and check if it hits a block or an entity.
  since 2023/10/09 1.20.2
  $ray
  input arguments
    blocks?: $blocks
    entities?: $entities
    selector?: $selector
    max_distance?: $max_distance
    on_block?: $run > command to run at the block the ray hits, aligned to the grid
    on_entity?: $run > command to run as and at the entity the ray hits
    on_entry?: $run > command to run at the point where the ray enters the nearest box it hits
  output success > whether a block or an entity stops the ray

feature function pierce > Cast a ray that goes through every block and entity it hits, until a command stops it.
  since 2026/10/25 26.3
  $ray
  input arguments
    blocks?: $provider
    entities?: $entities
    selector?: $selector
    max_distance?: $max_distance
    on_block?: $run > command to run at each block the ray hits, aligned to the grid: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_entity?: $run > command to run as and at each entity the ray hits: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_entry?: $run > command to run at each point where the ray enters a box, nearest first: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
    on_exit?: $run > command to run at each point where the ray leaves a box, right after its `on_entry`: the ray stops there unless it returns a non-zero value
  output success > whether a command stops the ray

feature predicate face/$face > Check if the ray enters the box it hits by its $face face. Use it in a command of the ray.
  since 2026/10/13 26.3
  output success > whether the $face face is hit

feature predicate flag/$flag > Check if the box the ray hits has the flag `$flag`, as its provider gives it. Use it in a command of the ray.
  since 2026/10/13 26.3
  output success > whether the box has the flag `$flag`

feature context_float_provider $point/distance > Get the distance from the origin of the ray to the point where it $point.verb what it hits. Use it in $point.where.
  since 2026/10/13 26.3
  output result: float @ 0.. > distance in blocks

feature context_float_provider $point/$axis > Get the $axis coordinate of the point where the ray $point.verb what it hits, relative to the block it hits, or to the feet of the entity it hits. Use it in $point.where.
  since 2026/10/19 26.3
  output result: float > $axis coordinate in blocks, from the $axis.side side of the block or from the feet of the entity

feature context_int_provider block/$axis > Get the $axis coordinate of the block the ray hits. Use it in a command of the ray.
  since 2026/10/19 26.3
  output result: int > $axis coordinate of the block
